      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: tighten control ui input validation [AI]",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where edge-case Control UI preview inputs and assistant media filenames were accepted more broadly than needed, which could produce unnecessary upstream requests or less predictable download headers.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis change tightens shared object-key filtering, validates GitHub preview repository names before any preview fetch, normalizes GitHub avatar URLs to a small deterministic request shape, and sanitizes assistant media filenames before building response headers. The patch keeps the existing Control UI and config merge behavior for valid inputs.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers should see the same behavior for normal GitHub issue and pull request previews and normal assistant media downloads. Invalid preview targets, unsafe avatar URLs, and unusual media filenames are now handled more conservatively.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAI-assisted change.\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/prototype-keys.test.ts src/config/merge-patch.proto-pollution.test.ts src/gateway/control-ui-github-preview.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/control-ui.http.test.ts -t 'sanitizes control characters|caps long'`\n\nRemote validation was not available in this environment: Blacksmith Testbox was missing its CLI and direct AWS Crabbox required broker login.\n",
